# Gu�a de ingenier�a

Resu�lvelo is a B2B marketplace (Next.js 16 App Router, React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind v4, shadcn/ui, Supabase, Zustand, Vitest). This Next.js version differs from training data. Before writing Next.js code, read the relevant guide in `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` and heed deprecation notices.

## Architecture

- Transport and UI live in `app/` (routes, layouts, Server Actions) and `components/` (`layout/`, `marketplace/`, `ui/`).
- Domain types live in `types/index.ts`.
- The data boundary is `lib/data.ts`: catalog and quote reads go through Supabase, with an automatic fallback to `lib/mock.ts` when `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` is missing or still the example placeholder. Do not query Supabase from components.
- `lib/supabase/client.ts`, `lib/supabase/server.ts`, and `lib/supabase/proxy.ts` are clients only.
- The cart is client-only Zustand in `lib/store/carrito.ts`, persisted in `localStorage`.
- Quote creation resolves provider and price on the server. Never trust prices or provider ids sent by the client.
- Authorization is Postgres Row Level Security in `supabase/schema.sql`. UI checks are not the authorization layer.
- Buyer flows: `app/(marketplace)/` catalog, cart, quotes. Provider flows: `app/(marketplace)/proveedor/`. Auth: `app/(auth)/`.

## Gate commands

| Command | What it checks | Shared state |
|---|---|---|
| `npm run test` | Vitest unit tests (`tests/`). Local only; no Supabase. | Does not mutate shared remote state. |
| `npm run lint` | ESLint. | Local. |
| `npm run typecheck` | Generates Next.js route types and checks TypeScript. | Writes `*.tsbuildinfo` (gitignored). |
| `npm run build` | Production Next.js build. | Writes `.next/`. |
| `npm run dev` | Dev server on port 3000. | Binds port 3000. |

A skipped test is not a pass. Do not claim a command passed unless you ran it and saw it pass.

## Shared resources

Parallel workers share this checkout. In one fan-out, assign each of these to at most one worker:

- `npm run dev` (port 3000)
- `npm run build` and `npm run typecheck` (they write compiler output)
- Applying `supabase/schema.sql` or `supabase/seed.sql` (one shared Supabase project)
- `npx vercel deploy` (production)

`npm run test` and `npm run lint` do not touch Supabase. Still do not run two copies of the same gate at once on this checkout.

Do not add npm dependencies unless the approved plan includes them. Do not commit `.env`, `.env.local`, or any secret. `.env.example` is the only env file that belongs in git.

UI, layout, routing, client state, or rendered-data changes need a browser pass of the affected flow before the work is called complete. If no browser is available, use the closest substitute (`npm run test`, or a request against the dev server) and say what was not verified.


